{"resourceIdentifier":"1765","resourceName":"Grouped Project for reducing emissions from deforestation and forest degradation-REDD-in the Regional Natural Park:Biological Corridor PNN Purace-PNN Cueva de los Guacharos","description":"The cluster/grouped Project for Reducing Emissions from Deforestation and Forest Degradation: “Regional Natural Park: Biological Corridor PNN Puracé – PNN Cueva de los Guácharos” (henceforward referred as REDD Huila – CB) is located in the Colombian Andes region. Which main objectives include the climate, community, and biodiversity: 1. Reduction of deforestation in the Project area, and associated GHG emissions 2. Conserve and enhance existing biodiversity, and increase the value of standing forest over time, in order to achieve conservation objectives.3. Facilitate the access to investment for the improvement of existing production systems, and increase the income of rural population and farmers.4. Ensure sustainability for the new production systems that farmers are going to invest in, and achieve markets and obtain the maximum benefit of their products (added value).5. To promote governance, monitoring and control, on a community basis, in conjunction with local environmental institutions, in order to ensure deforestation reductions in the area.PUBLIC COMMENT PERIOD:CCB Standards public comment period for validation – 07 February –  08 March 2020. No comments were received","location":{"latitude":1.764026,"longitude":-76.259782},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2024-11-11","endExclusive":"2024-12-12","endInclusive":"2024-12-11"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1765"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"HUILA"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Corporación Autónoma Regional del Río Grande de la Magdalena (CORMAGDALENA)"},{"type":"string",